What is the meaning of left continuity for a function, and how can it be proven in the context of a monotone non-decreasing and left continuous function $\phi:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ being related to a convex function $\Phi:(a,b)\to \mathbb{R}$ as stated in the following property:
\begin{equation}
\Phi(x)=\Phi(c)+\int_{c}^{x}\phi(t)dt : c\leq x\leq d......(1)
\end{equation}
Moreover, how can we geometrically visualize left continuity?
